 ## Decide what Pi can access
 
@@ -181,3 +182,25 @@ pi -e ~/.pi/agent/extensions/gondolin
 The extension mounts the host working folder at `/workspace` in the VM and overrides `read`, `write`, `edit`, `bash`, `grep`, `find`, and `ls`. File changes under `/workspace` write through to the host.
 
 Other extension tools still run on the host unless they explicitly delegate their operations. Review the [Gondolin example](../examples/extensions/gondolin/) before adding tools that could bypass the VM boundary.
+
+## Route tools through a Prized sandbox
+
+[Prized](https://prized.dev/docs/sandboxes) sandboxes are remote Firecracker micro-VMs. The [`@prized/pi`](https://github.com/prized-dev/integrations/tree/main/pi) extension keeps the Pi process, its credentials, and model calls on the host, and runs `bash`, `read`, `write`, `edit`, and `!` commands in a sandbox. Host environment variables are not forwarded into the sandbox.
+
+Your first prompt starts the sandbox and uploads the git working tree: tracked and new files that git does not ignore, up to 100 MiB packed. Changes stay in the sandbox until you apply them to the host with `/prized pull`. Prized deletes the sandbox, with anything not pulled, when its run time ends (60 minutes on the free tier, 24 hours by default on paid plans) or a week after it is left paused. Between turns the sandbox pauses with its memory, so a server the agent started is still running at the next command.
+
+### Install the extension
+
+```bash
+pi install npm:@prized/pi
+export PRIZED_API_KEY=<key from the Prized dashboard, API keys>
+```
+
+### Start Pi
+
+```bash
+cd /path/to/working-folder
+pi --prized
+```
+
+With `--prized`, `grep`, `find`, `ls`, and `powershell` are disabled because they would act on the host, and Pi skills are left out of the prompt; the agent searches with `bash` in the sandbox. Other extension tools still run on the host. See the [extension README](https://github.com/prized-dev/integrations/tree/main/pi#readme) for sandbox size, pause, and pull options.
